may not be the city's favorite team  anymore but the days of the cleveland  indians taking the field  are numbered it's official the team  threw a curveball this morning  by announcing they will change the name  to the guardians effective  at the end of the 2021 season the  decision ends 100 over 100 years of  indian's history  bob feller manny ramirez by the board so  to speak  and it follows a similar move made by  last year's washington  one-time redskins and now the washington  football club  formerly the redskins who changed their  name following a public  outcry they'll name make it another  official name soon  so what is the right call in these  politically correct times are these  teams abandoning their history  let's ask legendary washington redskins  quarterback  super bowl champion his own right author  of this book how to be a champion every  day it's excellent  joe theismann welcome joe i thought  you'd be perfect  you are proud of the history of the  redskins and now the washington football  club  did the cleveland indians make the right  move today you know brian i think it's a  sign of the times  socially i i really believe that this is  what uh we're dealing with  uh you see names being changed uh you're  never gonna get rid of the history i  mean we won three world champions as the  washington redskins  cleveland has had success as a franchise  as the cleveland indians  those are things i hope and pray will  remain but  i i say this to those young people that  are going to be a part of those  franchises going forward  it's your turn to create a new legacy  it's your  turn to create something under a new  name and like i said  it's it's a sign of the times that we're  living in it's the pressures that people  are under  whether it's economic pressure whether  it's outcries whatever it might be  um it's just something that is here and  to right cry over spilt milk just  wouldn't do any good  so i think you have to accept it move  forward with it gotcha um you know  there's a lot of history in cleveland  there was a lot of history with the  washington  franchise going all the way back what 87  years  but now it's time to i think have to  open our eyes and say okay now we're  moving to another era another time  and another place for young players so  here's the question uh they're talking  now about the  kansas city chiefs you know i didn't  think the word chief was a  insult i thought it showed leadership uh  braves  it's the way you fight a lot of people  thought the native american community is  not on the same page in this  do you expect this to be next well i'm  certainly gonna  i would assume that there's gonna be  conversations about it exactly what  happens i mean  let's take the florida state seminoles  as an example  basically the seminoles have basically  said don't touch our football team don't  touch florida state  we're not changing the name so that's a  group that has stood up and said it's  not going to happen  i don't know what's going to happen in  kansas city and i'm not sure what's  going to happen in atlanta  atlantis basically said we'll get rid of  the the chop  but we want to keep the name so you just  don't know  what pressure is going to come to bear  in the future  to ask these franchises to make the  changes that they'll be asked to make if  they are  we'll see if fighting irish some people  are challenging that and you can relate  to that as a notre dame grad and a  superstar there  let's move on and talk about the nfl  league you know quite well  they decided today they told all 32  clubs that the covet outbreaks  among unvaccinated players could result  in forfeiture of a game they're no  longer going to bend  if teams turn out with too many players  who are on the ir  because of uh getting covet 19. is this  the right move did the league have to  make this  proclamation uh well i think the league  has to make some type of a pro  proclamation brian but but who are you  penalizing if  you forfeit games you're penalizing the  players that have been vaccinated  so what sense does that make that if  there's a forfeiture  both those that have not been vaccinated  and those that have been vaccinated  now will be punished in accordance the  same way it just doesn't seem fair  here's to me there's only one possible  solution  to this situation and that is if you're  not vaccinated right  then you have to treat it like it was in  2020.  you're not going to be in the facility  you're not going to be on the football  team  we will get through this at some point  in time and yes i realize there's the  delta variants and all the other things  that we're talking about but at some  point in time this will be in our  rearview mirror  now the andre hopkins for example yeah  let me read this tweet for everyone at  home  uh here it is he's one of the finest  receivers in football he said quote when  this came out  never thought i would say this but being  in a position to hurt my team because i  don't want to partake  in the vaccine is making me question my  future in the nfl he went on to say he  deleted that tweet he wanted to say he  thinks he could play nine more years  do you understand where he's coming from  some people are reluctant to do it  yes i understand what people are  reluctant to to get vaccinated i have  friends of mine  that have basically said they don't want  to get the vaccination  you know the vaccination does not have  fda approval  the vaccination of the three that we've  talked about  basically have just been approved for  emergency use  now are we in an emergency situation in  this country i think that's the question  but from a player's perspective i still  believe in the freedoms of this country  to be able to choose what you want to  put in your body  and i think it's it's you know i respect  the individuals that are making that  decision  but if you're going to be a league and  you want to protect the  the players in the league you can't ask  guys that have already gone and gotten  vaccinated  to lose a paycheck right because of a  forfeiture  the only real solution would be if  you're not vaccinated  you can't be on the facility and you  can't be a practice and then you find  players that are  and then you move forward i mean it's  the only fair way to do it  and not penalize those that have been  vaccinated joe theismann we asked you to  talk about sports  and the vaccine and a pandemic and you  made the adjustment you're still great  at calling an audible thanks so much  brian thank you great catching up with  you hey sean hannity here hey  click here to subscribe to fox news  youtube page  and catch our hottest interviews and  most compelling analysis  you will not get it anywhere else

